1
00:01:11,200 --> 00:01:11,799
Liu Wei.

2
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:14,359
Liu Wei!

3
00:01:15,480 --> 00:01:16,599
Are you Liu Wei?

4
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:18,000
And you are?

5
00:01:18,079 --> 00:01:20,200
I'm the director of Liu Wendou's factory.

6
00:01:20,959 --> 00:01:21,760
About what happened to his family...

7
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:23,280
Director Wang told you already, right?

8
00:01:23,280 --> 00:01:24,159
Yes, he did.

9
00:01:24,719 --> 00:01:25,359
Say hello to your uncle.

10
00:01:25,480 --> 00:01:25,840
This is Xiao Tong.

11
00:01:25,840 --> 00:01:26,200
Hello, Uncle.

12
00:01:27,120 --> 00:01:27,480
Have a seat.

13
00:01:27,480 --> 00:01:27,840
Come on.

14
00:01:27,959 --> 00:01:28,680
Sit down.

15
00:01:29,079 --> 00:01:30,760
The boy is smart and sensible.

16
00:01:30,760 --> 00:01:31,959
He does well in school, too.

17
00:01:32,200 --> 00:01:34,120
His grandmother passed away,

18
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:35,239
and the relatives on that side...

19
00:01:35,239 --> 00:01:36,319
aren't willing to take him in.

20
00:01:36,760 --> 00:01:38,319
Since you're Xiao Liu's cousin,

21
00:01:38,319 --> 00:01:39,200
could you...?

22
00:01:40,599 --> 00:01:42,120
You see how my family is living.

23
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:45,040
I'm raising three kids on my own.

24
00:01:45,719 --> 00:01:47,760
Too many mouths, not enough rations.

25
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:50,319
Taking him in isn't a problem.

26
00:01:51,519 --> 00:01:53,120
Only, Director...

27
00:01:54,319 --> 00:01:57,319
could I take over the job post for him?

28
00:02:05,359 --> 00:02:06,200
Come on.

29
00:02:09,039 --> 00:02:09,400
Let's go.

30
00:02:17,319 --> 00:02:18,360
Come back to the factory with me.

31
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:19,840
It's going to be okay.

32
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:22,879
You have a long road ahead of you.

33
00:02:26,080 --> 00:02:27,360
There's bound to be a way.

34
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:30,000
Uncle,

35
00:02:30,759 --> 00:02:32,120
where did my dad go?

36
00:02:34,199 --> 00:02:35,240
Right now,

37
00:02:35,960 --> 00:02:36,680
you're still too young to understand.

38
00:02:36,680 --> 00:02:38,080
You'll understand when you grow up.

39
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,400
But Mom's dream was real that day.

40
00:02:41,639 --> 00:02:43,360
My dad isn't a bad person.

41
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:45,680
I believe the dream was real too.

42
00:02:47,240 --> 00:02:49,560
But a dream is still just a dream.

43
00:02:50,159 --> 00:02:51,360
Remember this, child.

44
00:02:52,280 --> 00:02:54,080
In life, we must follow the rules.

45
00:02:55,879 --> 00:02:57,879
Regulations are strict right now.

46
00:02:58,159 --> 00:02:59,639
Everything is punished severely.

47
00:03:01,680 --> 00:03:02,599
Your dad...

48
00:03:04,719 --> 00:03:06,039
is waiting for word.

49
00:03:06,840 --> 00:03:08,919
But I heard the men at the factory say

50
00:03:09,479 --> 00:03:11,120
that he's waiting for the death penalty.

51
00:03:14,680 --> 00:03:15,479
Xiao Tong,

52
00:03:16,400 --> 00:03:17,319
you know that

53
00:03:17,560 --> 00:03:19,879
I only have a daughter.

54
00:03:20,479 --> 00:03:21,159
By the way,

55
00:03:21,560 --> 00:03:23,000
she's in the same class as you.

56
00:03:24,080 --> 00:03:25,599
If you don't mind,

57
00:03:26,599 --> 00:03:28,159
you can stay with us for now.

58
00:03:28,840 --> 00:03:30,680
From now on, we're family.

59
00:03:32,039 --> 00:03:32,719
Don't worry.

60
00:03:33,159 --> 00:03:35,000
I won't let you go hungry.

61
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:38,400
We'll make sure you keep going to school.

62
00:03:41,840 --> 00:03:43,319
Living with me from now on,

63
00:03:43,879 --> 00:03:45,120
your name will be...

64
00:03:45,520 --> 00:03:46,439
Yan Tong.

65
00:03:49,159 --> 00:03:51,879
Could you be that child, Lawyer Yan Tong?

66
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:11,360
Now I understand.

67
00:04:15,560 --> 00:04:17,759
The secret hidden in this room

68
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:21,439
is the final case, The 14th Case.

69
00:04:21,920 --> 00:04:24,360
It's the crime your own father committed.

70
00:04:24,360 --> 00:04:24,879
Right?

71
00:04:27,839 --> 00:04:28,720
You once couldn't understand

72
00:04:28,720 --> 00:04:29,920
how there could be

73
00:04:30,279 --> 00:04:32,399
those ignorant, selfish criminals.

74
00:04:35,759 --> 00:04:38,120
Why make me study these 13 murder cases?

75
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:40,920
Tell me!

76
00:04:41,199 --> 00:04:42,720
What was it all for?

77
00:04:44,480 --> 00:04:46,279
Was it so I'd understand you better,

78
00:04:47,800 --> 00:04:49,680
or was it so that you

79
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:51,759
could face yourself once again?

80
00:04:52,399 --> 00:04:53,199
Fu Ting,

81
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:57,240
you've studied 13 homicide cases.

82
00:04:59,040 --> 00:04:59,839
Do you think

83
00:05:00,759 --> 00:05:02,000
a killer

84
00:05:02,759 --> 00:05:05,000
deserves to be understood?

85
00:05:13,920 --> 00:05:15,199
All these years,

86
00:05:16,800 --> 00:05:18,360
I worked hard to get into a top school,

87
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:19,399
studied abroad,

88
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:22,800
and read countless classic case files.

89
00:05:23,759 --> 00:05:26,240
I've heard too many motives,

90
00:05:26,680 --> 00:05:27,800
too many excuses.

91
00:05:28,720 --> 00:05:29,839
They say

92
00:05:31,399 --> 00:05:32,639
it was self-defense,

93
00:05:34,399 --> 00:05:36,399
because of their childhood,

94
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:39,360
because of depression,

95
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:40,240
or because of alcohol.

96
00:05:40,399 --> 00:05:41,680
Of course, I didn't believe

97
00:05:42,240 --> 00:05:43,560
any of their explanations.

98
00:05:44,879 --> 00:05:46,000
But in my heart,

99
00:05:47,879 --> 00:05:49,199
I could never forget.

100
00:05:52,839 --> 00:05:53,720
For me,

101
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:57,160
the first murder,

102
00:05:59,879 --> 00:06:01,600
the first killer,

103
00:06:03,560 --> 00:06:04,720
was my father.

104
00:06:07,720 --> 00:06:08,680
He wasn't a monster.

105
00:06:10,120 --> 00:06:11,680
Day in and day out,

106
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:14,079
cared for his bedridden wife for 6 years.

107
00:06:15,519 --> 00:06:16,519
Six whole years.

108
00:06:20,199 --> 00:06:21,079
Carrying her to bathe,

109
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:22,560
feeding her meals,

110
00:06:23,399 --> 00:06:24,160
and late into the night,

111
00:06:25,319 --> 00:06:26,079
listening to her

112
00:06:27,160 --> 00:06:29,120
groaning in agony,

113
00:06:30,959 --> 00:06:32,439
struggling and begging to die.

114
00:06:37,399 --> 00:06:38,399
He didn't run away,

115
00:06:40,360 --> 00:06:41,199
didn't cheat on her,

116
00:06:42,319 --> 00:06:43,199
and didn't complain.

117
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:45,800
He was just

118
00:06:49,759 --> 00:06:50,720
too tired.

119
00:06:51,560 --> 00:06:52,160
Truly,

120
00:06:54,360 --> 00:06:55,079
deeply exhausted.

121
00:07:00,279 --> 00:07:01,240
That night,

122
00:07:03,879 --> 00:07:06,079
he said he had a dream.

123
00:07:10,040 --> 00:07:11,040
He said she told him,

124
00:07:13,199 --> 00:07:14,480
"Please,

125
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:17,240
let me go."

126
00:07:22,920 --> 00:07:24,720
Did she really say those words?

127
00:07:26,439 --> 00:07:27,600
Who knows?

128
00:07:28,279 --> 00:07:29,319
But he believed it.

129
00:07:30,199 --> 00:07:31,759
And so, he did it.

130
00:07:32,879 --> 00:07:35,079
He thought he was fulfilling her wish,

131
00:07:35,079 --> 00:07:36,000
setting her free.

132
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,160
But the world

133
00:07:38,560 --> 00:07:39,680
said he had

134
00:07:42,399 --> 00:07:43,439
murdered his wife.

135
00:07:45,560 --> 00:07:46,959
I witnessed

136
00:07:48,160 --> 00:07:50,720
everything that night with my own eyes.

137
00:07:53,519 --> 00:07:54,319
That year...

138
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:57,360
That year,

139
00:08:00,360 --> 00:08:01,600
I was only seven.

140
00:08:09,439 --> 00:08:10,399
The next day,

141
00:08:11,079 --> 00:08:12,959
I told my grandmother about the dream.

142
00:08:14,240 --> 00:08:15,600
Father was taken away,

143
00:08:15,920 --> 00:08:17,160
and I,

144
00:08:18,720 --> 00:08:19,680
from that day on,

145
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:22,600
never again called him

146
00:08:26,399 --> 00:08:27,199
"Dad."

147
00:08:29,959 --> 00:08:32,320
I became his primary tainted witness,

148
00:08:32,840 --> 00:08:33,120
while I

149
00:08:36,120 --> 00:08:38,159
was the person he wanted to protect most.

150
00:08:39,519 --> 00:08:42,759
He never once defended himself,

151
00:08:42,759 --> 00:08:45,080
right until the gunshot rang out.

152
00:08:48,440 --> 00:08:49,240
The death penalty.

153
00:08:52,120 --> 00:08:55,120
I tried studying law

154
00:08:56,120 --> 00:08:58,080
to step into their world.

155
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:02,080
I didn't want to save anyone.

156
00:09:03,559 --> 00:09:05,200
I just wanted an answer to one question:

157
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:07,639
Human nature...

158
00:09:11,559 --> 00:09:13,279
Is it truly worth believing in?

159
00:09:29,639 --> 00:09:31,240
This is what is now

160
00:09:32,120 --> 00:09:35,600
my heaviest burden, The 14th Case.

161
00:09:38,240 --> 00:09:39,480
I once

162
00:09:40,879 --> 00:09:42,480
tried to destroy it,

163
00:09:43,799 --> 00:09:46,360
tried to bury it, but it...

164
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:49,279
It was always there.

165
00:09:53,039 --> 00:09:54,399
It would never truly go away.

166
00:10:00,240 --> 00:10:01,679
Later, I took the surname Yan.

167
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:04,039
I tried so hard

168
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:05,840
to forget everything in the past.

169
00:10:07,559 --> 00:10:08,600
I worked so hard

170
00:10:09,639 --> 00:10:11,639
to get into the best law school.

171
00:10:15,960 --> 00:10:16,879
I just...

172
00:10:18,840 --> 00:10:19,679
I was just...

173
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:26,000
In a sense,

174
00:10:27,720 --> 00:10:31,399
you're part of my search for the truth.

175
00:10:31,919 --> 00:10:35,480
You studied those 13 cases in depth.

176
00:10:36,279 --> 00:10:38,120
Now you know about The 14th Case.

177
00:10:38,360 --> 00:10:39,320
Can you tell me,

178
00:10:39,320 --> 00:10:40,519
if it were you,

179
00:10:43,679 --> 00:10:45,480
would you defend your father?

180
00:10:46,639 --> 00:10:47,519
If it were you,

181
00:10:48,240 --> 00:10:50,000
could you ever forgive

182
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:53,159
the childhood self who told the truth?

183
00:11:00,799 --> 00:11:02,000
But have you...

184
00:11:05,039 --> 00:11:07,399
Did you ever truly consider your mother?

185
00:11:11,879 --> 00:11:14,279
She was paralyzed for half her life.

186
00:11:16,159 --> 00:11:17,720
On some level,

187
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:20,360
she suffered even more than Yang Dongmei.

188
00:11:21,799 --> 00:11:23,480
I didn't dare.

189
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:27,320
I knew her pain.

190
00:11:28,519 --> 00:11:30,360
Life was worse than death for her.

191
00:11:30,360 --> 00:11:32,879
She didn't want to keep burdening us.

192
00:11:33,559 --> 00:11:34,360
Yet I...

193
00:11:36,240 --> 00:11:37,639
I spoke of that dream,

194
00:11:40,679 --> 00:11:41,879
sent my father away,

195
00:11:44,639 --> 00:11:46,159
and bid farewell to my mother forever.

196
00:11:48,480 --> 00:11:49,679
I was the one...

197
00:11:50,320 --> 00:11:52,600
who completely destroyed this family.

198
00:11:53,279 --> 00:11:55,200
Not to save anyone else.

199
00:11:55,200 --> 00:11:56,039
I was thinking...

200
00:11:56,799 --> 00:11:58,399
What if... what if,

201
00:11:58,960 --> 00:12:00,279
on that winter night,

202
00:12:00,320 --> 00:12:03,000
if someone could have

203
00:12:03,960 --> 00:12:04,840
for this...

204
00:12:05,360 --> 00:12:09,080
done something for this broken family?

205
00:12:13,080 --> 00:12:13,879
Maybe...

206
00:12:15,480 --> 00:12:16,600
Maybe the outcome

207
00:12:17,639 --> 00:12:19,360
would've been completely different.

208
00:12:30,360 --> 00:12:31,120
Still,

209
00:12:33,039 --> 00:12:34,200
I have to thank you.

210
00:12:35,320 --> 00:12:36,279
Thank me for what?

211
00:12:38,679 --> 00:12:39,840
For my father...

212
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:43,120
and my mother.

213
00:12:58,639 --> 00:13:00,320
In the next life, we'll live well.

214
00:13:01,759 --> 00:13:02,639
In this life,

215
00:13:04,159 --> 00:13:05,759
this is all I can do for you.

216
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:23,279
You once asked me

217
00:13:23,879 --> 00:13:25,320
if human nature is worth believing in.

218
00:13:26,399 --> 00:13:28,000
Now I want to tell you:

219
00:13:28,679 --> 00:13:29,399
It is.

220
00:13:30,279 --> 00:13:33,200
Even if it can be stubborn sometimes,

221
00:13:33,320 --> 00:13:34,480
and completely irrational,

222
00:13:35,559 --> 00:13:36,840
that's just how people are.

223
00:13:37,080 --> 00:13:40,600
We must learn to make peace and coexist.

224
00:13:41,399 --> 00:13:43,120
Human nature is also volatile.

225
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:46,360
It can collapse under certain conditions.

226
00:13:47,159 --> 00:13:48,559
The purpose of the law

227
00:13:48,559 --> 00:13:51,200
is to ensure in the direst situations,

228
00:13:51,200 --> 00:13:52,840
people still hold on to reason.

229
00:13:53,679 --> 00:13:55,519
They aren't monsters born of evil;

230
00:13:55,759 --> 00:13:57,600
they're simply people who lost control.

231
00:13:57,919 --> 00:13:59,279
What we must remember is

232
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:02,000
the real danger isn't criminals,

233
00:14:02,600 --> 00:14:04,440
but believing that we

234
00:14:04,440 --> 00:14:06,440
could never become

235
00:14:07,320 --> 00:14:09,320
the one who picks up the knife.

236
00:16:18,159 --> 00:16:19,279
Lao Wang.

237
00:16:19,759 --> 00:16:21,000
Yes, I'm resigning.

238
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:25,919
"Resigning" isn't quite accurate.

239
00:16:26,279 --> 00:16:28,120
I want to be a public interest lawyer,

240
00:16:28,840 --> 00:16:30,120
travel across the country,

241
00:16:30,759 --> 00:16:32,279
and become a Grassroots legal educator.

242
00:16:33,240 --> 00:16:34,519
Only by going deep into society

243
00:16:35,159 --> 00:16:37,720
can we truly prevent crime.
